# Normalise to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# `rustfmt.toml` sets `newline_style = "Unix"`, so a checkout that converted to
# CRLF would fail `cargo fmt --check` on a clean clone, on Windows only, which
# is the worst place for a gate to disagree with itself. Setting it here rather
# than relying on each developer's `core.autocrlf` keeps the rule with the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF whatever the platform: CRLF makes a `#!` line
# unparseable and the failure ("bad interpreter") does not name the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Firmware images, disk images and anything else with a fixed byte layout.
*.fd binary
*.img binary
*.bin binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary

# Fuzz corpora: arbitrary bytes, chosen for the shape they have. `text=auto`
# classifies the entries without a NUL byte as text and would rewrite their
# line endings, changing the input the target replays.
src/tests/fuzz/corpus/** binary
src/tests/fuzz/artifacts/** binary

# Fonts: TrueType outlines, not text.
*.ttf binary
